  "text": "Harvest Season - Wisconsin Corn Agronomy Corn Agronomy Monday, October 26, 2026 Where science meets the field Search Subscribe Home Season Management Silage Crops Programs Calculators Blog Twitter Distance Diagnosis Silage Drydown Pre-Season Planting Season In-Season Harvest Season Post-Season WI Agriculture Hybrid selection Soil Fertility Management Harvesting/Storage Ensiling Quality and Feeding Economics/Budgets Grains Legume Pulses Oil Seeds Other Research Extension Hybrid Trials PEPS On-Farm Testing Team Grains Team Forage Publications Home | Management | Harvest Season Season Management Pre-Season Planting Season In-Season Harvest Season Post-Season WI Agriculture Harvest Season Evaluating Fields Silage harvesting Timing harvest Drydown Days HMC, HMEC, Snaplage Dry Grain harvesting Combine adjustments Down corn Storage Harvest Season Originally written February 1, 2006 | Last updated March 03, 2014 Corn harvesting begins with some fields green-chopped and quickly proceeds to silage harvest, high moisture corn and dry corn harvest. Often stover is harvested after dry grain harvest and used as bedding material. Increasingly, corn fields are being looked at for biomass harvest as well. This season is an important time of the year when all of the challenges of the growing eason come to fruition. It is truly when farmers \"make their money\" and the effects of their management decisions during the season are realized. If you would like to subscribe (or unsubscribe) to updates during the growing season, click here . © 1994- 2026",
